  "rationale" : "The second documentation-grade happy path and the only fixture covering UTF-8, apostrophes, and a numeric-looking string that must stay a string. Combines a uniform object array with a scalar-only nested map so array and object inference must both be right in the same document.",
  "catchesBugClass" : "Charset and escaping regressions; numeric coercion of numeric-looking strings inside arrays; object-versus-array misclassification when both appear as siblings; boolean fidelity through the array-free path.",
  "cannotCatch" : "It says nothing about what happens when preferences gains an array-valued key - that is one character apart in risk. It also cannot catch element misalignment, since both addresses declare an identical field set.",
  "predicted" : {
    "classification" : "LOSSLESS",
    "detail" : "addresses is detected as an array; preferences holds only scalars and booleans so it stays an object. The postal code survives as a String because serializeArray writes it with JSON quotes."
  },
